bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    seed_interp_local_to_i64_unwrap_shifts_by_tag_2026_11_09, 1, "Repro (bin/simple.exe Rust seed, 34874368 bytes 2026-11-09 12:58, run inside the repo): val d = "20672".to_i64(); print d! -> 2584 (=20672>>3, a tag shift), d! == 20672 -> false. val parts = ".tmp.20672.x".split("."); val o = if parts.len() >= 4: parts[2].to_i64() else: None; o! -> 2584. Correct: fn pick(s, ok) -> i64?: if ok: s.to_i64() else: None then pick(...)! -> 20672; "20672".to_i64() ?? 0 -> 20672. Same probe: "abc".to_i64() == None printed false (check separately)."
    seed_interp_local_to_i64_unwrap_shifts_by_tag_2026_11_09, 2, "Impact: any safe-code pid/int parse using the local-then-! pattern compares a shifted value; seen as recover_v1 deleting a live-owner staging dir under a probe. Native/JIT behaviour not yet checked. Workaround: use ?? <default>."
    seed_interp_local_to_i64_unwrap_shifts_by_tag_2026_11_09, 3, "Fix PR #8086: seed HIR lower_try treats ! on a bare raw scalar (I64 etc.) as identity; JIT red 2584 -> green 20672. Pending native verification."

